WEBVTT

00:01.060 --> 00:05.880
Well then, may I make my request now?

00:05.880 --> 00:08.860
It's for Schwarz Vulf,

00:09.860 --> 00:11.120
Library,

00:11.120 --> 00:12.240
SF-Zoo,

00:12.710 --> 00:14.990
and us in Wolf-Gang.

00:17.220 --> 00:19.000
I'd like us to form a Clan Alliance.

00:20.080 --> 00:24.500
#29: TOWARDS THE SKIES,
DREAMING THE IMPOSSIBLE

00:35.180 --> 00:36.270
I see.

00:37.310 --> 00:39.220
So that's her aim from the start.

00:40.400 --> 00:42.440
That's fine by me.

00:42.440 --> 00:46.070
SF-Zoo's request is still
not done yet, though.

00:46.070 --> 00:49.110
I have no reason to refuse either.

00:49.110 --> 00:52.740
I doubt it'll change
our activities by much.

00:53.220 --> 00:55.410
Very well, Pencilgon.

00:55.410 --> 00:57.040
I'll play along with you.

00:57.870 --> 00:59.480
I have no problem, either.

00:59.480 --> 01:01.870
I'd like to make
that proposal myself too.

01:03.000 --> 01:05.340
Let's forge an alliance.

01:22.100 --> 01:28.070
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

02:37.470 --> 02:39.390
It's finally over!

02:39.390 --> 02:41.770
Why are you acting like
you actually did something?

02:41.770 --> 02:44.060
All you did was just sit there.

02:44.060 --> 02:47.690
It took a lot of work
just to catch you, you know?

02:48.150 --> 02:51.570
Did you know people call you
"Tsuchinoko" on the internet?

02:51.570 --> 02:52.910
Where did that come from?

02:52.910 --> 02:55.070
They need to stop
giving me weird nicknames.

02:55.070 --> 02:59.530
But still, don't you think
you give up too much info?

02:59.530 --> 03:03.800
You mean info on Lycagon in exchange
for support for undoing my Mark?

03:03.800 --> 03:06.790
It's just her movement pattern.
Might as well give it for free.

03:06.790 --> 03:07.790
You're wrong.

03:09.420 --> 03:12.650
As a pro gamer,
I have to tell you this.

03:12.650 --> 03:16.220
Unlike in old games
that you only play on screen,

03:16.220 --> 03:19.850
in this era of Full-Dive games,
just knowing your opponent's moves

03:19.850 --> 03:22.430
gives you more advantages than you think.

03:22.870 --> 03:24.730
Especially with Unique Monsters.

03:24.730 --> 03:28.190
They're not some story bosses
every player would face.

03:28.190 --> 03:29.880
The info on them is priceless.

03:29.880 --> 03:32.980
Removing the status alignment,
which can be worked out if you try hard,

03:32.980 --> 03:34.820
is not exactly a good deal.

03:34.820 --> 03:37.200
Well, I guess you're right.

03:37.640 --> 03:41.830
Yeah, Schwarz Vulf did seem
to have an insight on us.

03:41.830 --> 03:46.160
Library aside, SF-Zoo is a problem.

03:46.870 --> 03:49.000
They're a pack of locusts.

03:49.000 --> 03:52.670
I doubt they know the difference
between NPCs and monsters.

03:53.230 --> 03:56.340
Just imagine what'll happen
if they get a pass ticket into Rabitz.

03:57.340 --> 03:59.680
They'd be on a mad spree of cuddling.

04:01.350 --> 04:05.770
I won't pry on what kinda
Unique Scenario you're hiding...

04:06.390 --> 04:09.190
But at the very least,
I hope you don't do anything stupid

04:09.190 --> 04:12.270
and let it fall into
someone else's hands, okay?

04:13.350 --> 04:14.900
That's my intention.

04:15.860 --> 04:21.030
But well, I accomplished my original goal,
so I'm good for now.

04:21.030 --> 04:23.240
You mean that Clan alliance thing?

04:23.240 --> 04:23.910
Yes!

04:24.370 --> 04:30.250
Now we can access the facilities
and rights that the other allied Clans have!

04:30.830 --> 04:34.170
I didn't expect every
one of them would say yes.

04:34.170 --> 04:35.670
From their perspective,

04:35.670 --> 04:39.720
it'll be like "We'll give you some favor,
so give us some info."

04:39.720 --> 04:42.470
But of course, we won't
give it up that easily!

04:42.470 --> 04:45.970
We have five cards
in our hands right now.

04:45.970 --> 04:47.100
One.

04:47.100 --> 04:51.350
By being the first group
to complete an EX Unique Scenario,

04:51.350 --> 04:54.180
we obtained information on Bahamut.

04:54.180 --> 04:55.480
Two.

04:55.480 --> 05:00.990
We've got access to Inventoria
and the assorted Legacy Weapons there.

05:01.570 --> 05:02.490
Three.

05:02.870 --> 05:05.990
We have de-facto exclusive access
to the Ancient Craftsman job

05:05.990 --> 05:08.830
that is only possessed by Bilac so far.

05:08.830 --> 05:10.330
Four.

05:10.330 --> 05:14.170
Sunraku has access to Rabitz
and info on the existence of Cat-siths

05:14.170 --> 05:17.880
and all other things
in relation to Rabitz.

05:18.550 --> 05:19.630
Five.

05:20.130 --> 05:25.780
We have an inside line on accessing
the next EX Unique Scenario.

05:27.100 --> 05:30.230
Simply hinting that we have
those cards gives us advantages.

05:30.690 --> 05:33.940
You can control or even kill people
with just information.

05:33.940 --> 05:38.780
Our new Clan consisting of only three
has game-leading clans serving us,

05:38.780 --> 05:43.950
keeping us one step ahead
of even die-hard gamers.

05:45.950 --> 05:50.250
Don't you think that's about
the funniest thing ever?

05:53.910 --> 05:56.460
You're making your evil face
again there, Pencilgon.

05:56.940 --> 06:01.090
I resorted to the stick too much
in United Rounds, after all.

06:01.090 --> 06:03.720
Time to switch gears
and use the carrot more.

06:03.720 --> 06:10.310
I bet we sound like some evil mastermind
who'll eventually get raided by other players.

06:10.720 --> 06:14.230
When that happens, I'll sell you
guys out and flee to Rabitz.

06:14.230 --> 06:15.150
Whoa, man.

06:16.310 --> 06:19.320
Well, we'll split off for now.

06:19.320 --> 06:22.110
Let us know if anything happens.

06:22.110 --> 06:25.280
You better not run
the next time we call you.

06:25.280 --> 06:27.280
Yeah, yeah. Just go.

06:27.280 --> 06:28.580
Sure, sure.

06:28.580 --> 06:29.580
See ya.

06:29.580 --> 06:31.410
I wanna log out and eat soon.

06:31.410 --> 06:34.290
Lack of sleep is bad for your skin.

06:38.670 --> 06:42.340
Come to think of it,
Emul didn't come back until the end.

06:42.880 --> 06:46.570
I'm curious about Bilac's progress, too.
I guess I'll go to Rabitz.

06:46.570 --> 06:49.970
But to do that, I need to get myself
killed to respawn at the save point...

06:53.520 --> 06:54.810
All right!

06:54.810 --> 06:56.900
If I gotta meet them again anyway,

06:56.900 --> 07:00.900
I'll farm their drops like crazy
before I go to Rabitz!

07:01.400 --> 07:05.780
Maybe I can score their stinger this time.

07:20.620 --> 07:22.880
C'mon! Follow me!

07:32.390 --> 07:36.690
I'll farm your tasty drop before
I death-warp myself back to Rabitz!

07:44.400 --> 07:46.240
All right, now's the time.

07:46.860 --> 07:49.660
TRANSFER: INVENTORY SPACE
Enter Travel!

07:51.160 --> 07:54.790
INVENTORY SPACE
Woah! That was too easy!

07:54.790 --> 08:00.440
Their broken parts should be
scattered all over the area by now!

08:00.440 --> 08:03.380
Now, time to come back and collect it!

08:03.380 --> 08:04.960
Let's go! Exit Travel!

08:04.960 --> 08:06.760
TRANSFER: REALITY

08:14.720 --> 08:16.730
No materials dropped?

08:17.110 --> 08:18.520
Why?

08:18.520 --> 08:21.230
I perfectly timed my return!

08:21.230 --> 08:23.610
Did they stop before they clashed?

08:23.610 --> 08:26.320
Their AI wasn't that smart!

08:26.750 --> 08:28.520
What the heck is going on?

08:39.120 --> 08:41.920
SUNRAKU

08:43.000 --> 08:45.050
An ambush?!

08:45.050 --> 08:48.890
That's totally different
from their behavior before!

08:48.890 --> 08:52.050
Don't tell me...
Those darn admins...

08:52.050 --> 08:57.350
You silently updated the game,
didn't you?!

09:02.310 --> 09:04.940
RABITZ INN

09:08.440 --> 09:10.450
LOGGING OUT

09:13.700 --> 09:15.450
Are you kidding me?

09:20.710 --> 09:22.670
Real-Time Update.

09:22.670 --> 09:25.840
"Fixed several monsters'
movement patterns."

09:26.360 --> 09:28.590
I'd figured it'll happen sooner or later,

09:28.590 --> 09:31.340
but damn it, why now?!

09:31.340 --> 09:33.220
It was my way to earn quick bucks

09:33.220 --> 09:37.600
and I just had the idea to kill them
with this "friendly fire" method.

09:37.600 --> 09:41.810
Killing regular enemies to level up
is getting inefficient, too.

09:41.810 --> 09:46.480
In that sense, the Crystal Scorpions
were a perfect target.

09:47.130 --> 09:50.530
Now I have to radically
adjust my plans.

09:50.530 --> 09:52.860
Now I can't use the "friendly fire" way,

09:52.860 --> 09:55.240
there's no way I can
beat them straight on...

09:55.700 --> 09:58.600
Oops, that was close...

10:00.730 --> 10:02.170
Gravity...

10:02.830 --> 10:05.960
That's it! The physics engine!

10:05.960 --> 10:09.380
Pairing that up with their AI...

10:09.380 --> 10:10.510
It could work!

10:10.510 --> 10:12.470
I can kill them with this!

10:12.910 --> 10:15.220
It's a Newton's Apple moment!

10:16.970 --> 10:20.270
But that alone won't be enough.

10:20.270 --> 10:21.560
Is there any other?

10:21.560 --> 10:25.640
Some kind of breakthrough
that I can use...

10:26.480 --> 10:27.610
This is it.

10:27.610 --> 10:29.400
SKY WALKER - UNLOCK: EVOLVED FROM MOON JUMPER
Sky Walker!

10:29.400 --> 10:30.610
EFFECT: PERFORM A SECOND JUMP IN THE AIR

10:30.610 --> 10:33.570
I could beat them with this skill!

10:33.570 --> 10:36.160
I just need to analyze
the Crystal Scorpions' AI patterns

10:36.160 --> 10:39.200
through trial and error,
and it'll be perfect!

10:40.620 --> 10:44.580
Those admins might think
they've conquered me with this update,

10:44.580 --> 10:45.960
but it's not enough!

10:45.960 --> 10:48.710
This ain't enough to bend me!

10:48.710 --> 10:52.760
I'll find more exploits for you to fix,
so prepare yourself!

10:56.970 --> 10:58.470
HIZUTOME

10:58.470 --> 11:01.970
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON
HIZUTOME

11:02.980 --> 11:04.100
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

11:04.100 --> 11:06.980
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON
Oh, Mr. Sunraku. You're back!

11:06.980 --> 11:10.900
Hey, Emul. How did your talk
with your brother go?

11:10.900 --> 11:15.820
Big brother Aydward said he'll think
about it, so he wants you to wait.

11:15.820 --> 11:16.740
I see.

11:17.120 --> 11:20.660
Also, Sis Bee asked
you to come to her forge.

11:20.660 --> 11:21.830
Oh!

11:21.830 --> 11:25.160
All right! Let's kick this off
with Bilac first!

11:26.210 --> 11:28.210
Let's go, Emul!

11:28.210 --> 11:30.670
You sound so full of energy, Mr. Sunraku.

11:30.670 --> 11:32.300
Did something good happen?

11:32.300 --> 11:33.840
Oh, you can tell?

11:33.840 --> 11:37.300
I got to my friend's house
but got my ass kicked.

11:37.300 --> 11:40.260
And I thought up a good way
to settle the score.

11:40.930 --> 11:46.390
They're kinda shy,
so they'll come to kill me in group.

11:46.390 --> 11:49.230
Are they really your friends?

11:51.770 --> 11:53.900
About time you showed up.

11:53.900 --> 11:56.200
Whip up your Legacy Weapon, will ya?

11:56.200 --> 12:00.660
What?! So you are supposed
to wear that on your head?

12:00.660 --> 12:02.530
So I was right!

12:02.530 --> 12:05.790
Yeah, I got the general gist of it.

12:05.790 --> 12:08.460
I'll use this to examine Legacy Weapon

12:08.460 --> 12:12.840
and study the forging
of the era of Divinity!

12:12.840 --> 12:14.340
Hmm...

12:16.340 --> 12:19.840
NON-STANDARD ARMAMENT: CONVERGING WEAPON
COMET CATAPULT

12:20.970 --> 12:23.180
Wow!

12:23.180 --> 12:24.680
Will that work?

12:24.680 --> 12:26.100
All right!

12:26.100 --> 12:29.190
Come back tomorrow morning!
I'll warp this up before then!

12:29.190 --> 12:33.170
Got it!
Feel free to break it apart or whatever!

12:33.170 --> 12:35.320
I need you to become
an Ancient Craftsman, ASAP!

12:36.110 --> 12:37.900
About that...

12:38.960 --> 12:41.240
Can I ask you a favor?

12:43.120 --> 12:46.330
Once I become an Ancient Craftsman,

12:46.330 --> 12:51.290
I should be able to make new weapons
with the skills I learned.

12:51.290 --> 12:53.750
You can make Legacy Weapons?

12:53.750 --> 12:57.590
Ancient Craftsman could not only
repair them, but make them too?

12:57.590 --> 12:59.010
Amazing!

12:59.010 --> 13:00.690
That's the thing.

13:00.690 --> 13:04.600
Remember those Crystal Scorpion
materials you brought here before?

13:04.600 --> 13:07.890
I want to use those to make
a brand-new Legacy Weapon!

13:07.890 --> 13:10.730
Crystal Scorpion materials...

13:10.730 --> 13:14.190
I know full well how hard it is to get.

13:14.190 --> 13:17.530
And this ain't like making
any normal weapon.

13:17.530 --> 13:19.360
I'm bound to screw up a lot.

13:20.070 --> 13:25.200
That's why I'll need a heck a lot of material,
and likely waste a heap of it.

13:26.740 --> 13:30.540
But my blacksmith soul's telling me.

13:31.080 --> 13:35.710
It says if I use those materials,
I'll be able to make my finest craft yet!

13:41.180 --> 13:42.340
I beg you!

13:43.300 --> 13:45.920
Take a risk on me, okay?!

13:51.110 --> 13:52.530
Don't be silly.

13:55.520 --> 14:00.530
Trial and error is a given
when you're tackling something new.

14:00.530 --> 14:01.900
It's no biggie.

14:01.900 --> 14:03.430
Use all you need.

14:06.410 --> 14:08.740
Thanks! I owe you one!

14:08.740 --> 14:11.500
Good for you, Sis Bee!

14:11.500 --> 14:14.600
So, what do you want me to make?
A set of twinblades?

14:15.170 --> 14:16.670
Twinblades...

14:16.670 --> 14:21.260
But I already have three pairs of those...

14:22.720 --> 14:23.500
Nah.

14:24.590 --> 14:28.850
I'd like to broaden my combat options.
I'll go with that instead.

14:29.310 --> 14:30.250
"That"?

14:35.560 --> 14:39.440
So where are we going next?

14:39.440 --> 14:41.070
We'll go leveling up.

14:41.540 --> 14:43.280
But before that...

14:44.070 --> 14:47.570
Oh, Emul and bird-man.
It's been a while.

14:47.570 --> 14:49.910
Long time no see, Peatz!

14:49.910 --> 14:52.330
I'm glad to find you here.

14:52.330 --> 14:54.710
I was hoping you could
buy something from me.

14:54.710 --> 14:56.330
Sure thing. Show me.

14:57.290 --> 15:00.590
I got this from Road of Past Glories.

15:01.590 --> 15:02.840
Let's see...

15:02.840 --> 15:06.180
Oh! It's Denier Sword Idol!

15:06.180 --> 15:09.010
I'll give you a bunch for this!
They're some rare stuff!

15:09.010 --> 15:10.470
Really?!

15:10.470 --> 15:12.180
Okay...

15:12.180 --> 15:13.930
How about 300,000 mahni?

15:13.930 --> 15:15.200
300,000?!

15:16.020 --> 15:19.900
For something like this?
I just cannot see it.

15:19.900 --> 15:23.280
If you got some idols modeled
after the Seven Colossi,

15:23.280 --> 15:25.990
I'll give ya a nice deal,
so bring them to me, okay?

15:25.990 --> 15:27.660
S-Sure.

15:27.660 --> 15:29.950
Idols, huh...

15:29.950 --> 15:32.410
I bet there are many versions of this...

15:32.910 --> 15:36.790
Oh no! My collector spirit is calling me!

15:39.290 --> 15:41.550
SPELLBOOKS

15:41.550 --> 15:45.090
You really bought me a new spellbook!

15:45.090 --> 15:47.470
Now I can cast a new magic!

15:47.470 --> 15:49.550
I'm so glad I asked for it!

15:49.550 --> 15:52.310
Gotta thank the unexpected extra income.

15:52.310 --> 15:56.040
I also wanted some more
assist magic, so it's perfect.

15:56.040 --> 15:58.060
Now then...

15:58.060 --> 16:02.820
Let's get prepared for the battle
against the Crystal Scorpions!

16:02.820 --> 16:04.480
Gotta level up first!

16:04.480 --> 16:09.410
We'll go to the Inner Canyon of Ancient Souls
and kill a bunch of undead!

16:09.410 --> 16:11.660
Let's go, Emul!

16:11.660 --> 16:15.040
My new magic's aching to be cast!

16:15.830 --> 16:17.830
Don't worry, Bilac.

16:17.830 --> 16:22.040
I'll get you more materials
than you could ever use up!

16:22.710 --> 16:24.960
INNER CANYON OF ANCIENT SOULS

16:24.960 --> 16:27.130
Wait, goddammit!

16:27.130 --> 16:29.930
Give me your freaking EXP!

16:29.930 --> 16:31.930
WYVERN ZOMBIE

16:31.930 --> 16:34.720
Get him, Emul!
Don't let him escape!

16:34.720 --> 16:35.430
Yessir!

16:35.810 --> 16:37.850
Magic Chain!

16:42.730 --> 16:44.610
Good job, Emul!

16:44.610 --> 16:48.700
The best thing about this magic
is that not only does it bind the target,

16:48.700 --> 16:51.280
but it also makes the target
do the "struggle" animation!

16:51.280 --> 16:56.540
With this, defeating feeling foes
is a heck lot easier!

16:56.540 --> 16:58.540
Glowing Pierce!

16:59.540 --> 17:01.540
GLOWING PIERCE

17:03.290 --> 17:05.170
One done!

17:05.170 --> 17:07.050
And more to come!

17:08.340 --> 17:11.010
Buying the spellbook was
the right choice after all!

17:11.010 --> 17:13.050
I'll take good care of it.

17:13.050 --> 17:17.140
Now then, let's hunt down
as many as we can like this.

17:17.140 --> 17:20.730
I gotta level up and get
that skill I'm aiming for.

17:23.520 --> 17:27.230
I was getting bored hunting
those wimps for their lousy EXPs.

17:27.820 --> 17:30.030
So I'm glad to run into you again.

17:30.030 --> 17:32.030
Dullahan General.

17:32.030 --> 17:34.030
RARE ENEMY
DULLAHAN GENERAL

17:34.030 --> 17:35.580
Let's go.

17:35.580 --> 17:36.910
Anytime.

17:38.450 --> 17:41.920
In SLF, whenever you gain a level,

17:42.490 --> 17:47.880
you will learn new skills or have
your old ones boosted or evolved.

17:48.550 --> 17:51.300
Whether you will learn new skills or not

17:51.300 --> 17:54.550
depends on how much battle
experience you've had prior.

17:54.550 --> 17:59.060
And I haven't gained a single level
ever since I fought Wethermon.

17:59.060 --> 18:00.140
Which means...

18:00.140 --> 18:00.850
Emul!

18:00.850 --> 18:02.890
Magic Chain!

18:06.480 --> 18:09.230
All the battle experience
I had until then...

18:09.860 --> 18:12.280
My understanding and awakening of skills...

18:12.280 --> 18:14.490
...are all packed into this single level!

18:14.490 --> 18:16.740
Heroic Fall!

18:16.740 --> 18:18.370
What is that?

18:18.370 --> 18:21.770
A random attack name I came up with!

18:25.500 --> 18:28.300
Rest in peace, Dullahan.

18:34.430 --> 18:35.930
SKILLS EVOLVED
NEW SKILLS LEARNED

18:35.930 --> 18:37.430
NEW SKILL
CLEAVER

18:37.430 --> 18:38.930
NEW SKILL
TEN COUNTER

18:38.930 --> 18:40.430
NEW SKILL
SHOCKWAVE FIST LV.1

18:40.430 --> 18:41.930
NEW SKILL
POWER SLASH LV.1

18:41.930 --> 18:43.440
SKILL EVOLVED
BOUNDLESS SLASH→BOUNDLESS MASSACRE

18:43.440 --> 18:44.940
SKILL EVOLVED
SIX-BOAT LEAP→SEVEN-BOAT LEAP

18:49.650 --> 18:51.190
Hehe, welcome to the team.

18:51.190 --> 18:51.860
SKILL EVOLVED: MOON JUMPER→SKY WALKER

18:51.860 --> 18:53.400
SKILL EVOLVED: MOON JUMPER→SKY WALKER
Sky Walker.

18:53.400 --> 18:54.200
SKILL EVOLVED: MOON JUMPER→SKY WALKER

18:57.240 --> 19:00.160
What? You're leaving me behind again?

19:00.160 --> 19:02.830
I'm just going out for a little solo trip.

19:02.830 --> 19:05.830
Geez, all right.

19:05.830 --> 19:08.000
There's been a lot of that lately.

19:08.000 --> 19:12.210
She sure is a little more amenable today.
Is it because I bought her that spellbook?

19:12.760 --> 19:15.380
Should I wait for you in Rabitz?

19:15.380 --> 19:17.550
Nah, umm...

19:18.100 --> 19:22.680
Come meet me again in this alley
right after sunrise, okay?

19:22.680 --> 19:24.560
Okay.

19:29.190 --> 19:30.730
That's right.

19:30.730 --> 19:34.680
This time I'm not planning to
return to Rabitz by dying.

19:39.700 --> 19:42.450
Sorry to keep you waiting,
Crystal Scorpions.

19:42.450 --> 19:44.330
I'm all ready now.

19:44.330 --> 19:46.920
Time to say your prayers.

19:51.500 --> 19:52.920
Now then...

19:53.510 --> 19:57.880
The physics engine that defines
the physics in this world...

19:57.880 --> 20:00.180
This engine applies to everything.

20:08.850 --> 20:09.860
NITRO GAIN - IGNITION - TRANSIENT

20:12.230 --> 20:15.360
Okay, follow me! We're going
full throttle from the get-go!

20:16.990 --> 20:19.530
C'mon! C'mon! Wake up guys!

20:19.530 --> 20:21.780
It's time for a party!

20:21.780 --> 20:24.080
In SLF, unlike your average trash games,

20:24.080 --> 20:27.000
apples fall to the ground,

20:27.000 --> 20:30.750
and if you hit someone from behind,
they'll stagger forward.

20:35.800 --> 20:39.050
The physics engine
simulates the real world

20:39.050 --> 20:42.350
and accurately replicates
the gravity and momentum!

20:47.600 --> 20:50.230
And that "common sense"
is what's about to kill you!

20:50.230 --> 20:56.820
I have no chance of winning
if I fight them head-on.

20:56.820 --> 20:57.690
SEVEN-BOAT LEAP

20:57.690 --> 20:59.400
So...

21:02.950 --> 21:05.330
Kill yourself.

21:12.710 --> 21:16.670
One of you could've hit
the brakes well enough,

21:16.670 --> 21:19.380
but not with that many of you!

21:19.380 --> 21:21.340
It'll not be able to
support all your weight.

21:25.010 --> 21:26.470
Fall to death.

21:26.470 --> 21:30.520
It kills anyone, NPCs,
players, and monsters.

21:30.520 --> 21:32.770
A death sentence by the physics engine.

21:33.170 --> 21:37.030
But I'll defy that law of physics!

21:38.400 --> 21:40.740
I "step" on the air...

21:43.910 --> 21:46.590
and make a one-time-only jump!

21:50.120 --> 21:52.580
It lets me do a double jump!

21:52.580 --> 21:56.130
That's the power of Sky Walker!

21:59.970 --> 22:02.970
I call this "Scorpion Fall."

22:02.970 --> 22:04.470
SCORPION FALL

22:06.970 --> 22:11.390
Operation to mass kill Crystal Scorpions...
is a huge success!
